# Which Akku site this app points at. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# Nothing about the POLICY belongs here — purposes, legal bases and expiry windows are all read from
# whatever the console has published for this site key. These only say WHERE to read it from and WHO
# is asking.
#
# There is deliberately no default for any of the three. A hostname committed here means a fresh clone
# with no environment silently writes consent decisions into somebody's production site.

# Base URL of the Akku API, e.g. https://consent.example.com
VITE_AKKU_API_HOST=

# The site's public site_key. Public by design: it resolves server-side to an org and a site.
VITE_AKKU_SITE_KEY=

# The registered application id (console -> site -> App keys), and the `iss` every Subject Token
# carries. Safe in the browser bundle — it is already inside every token this app holds.
#
# ALL THREE ARE REQUIRED. Miss any one and AKKU_CONFIGURED is false, no ConsentProvider is mounted,
# and every consent surface renders nothing. The preference centre says so on screen; a collection
# point is simply silent.
VITE_AKKU_APP_ID=

# OPTIONAL. Where `vite dev` should forward /api/subject-token, because it cannot run the serverless
# function itself. Defaults to the deployment, which signs for the same site and application. Point it
# at a local signer if you hold the private key yourself.
VITE_TOKEN_ORIGIN=
